The Go port in this directory (formerly tiktoken-go-fast) is a derivative of pkoukk/tiktoken-go.

  Upstream:   https://github.com/pkoukk/tiktoken-go
  Fork point: 200cf60 ("Merge pull request #72 from kuzminT/Fix_empty_cache_error")
  Licence:    MIT, retained unmodified in LICENSE

Changes from upstream:

  - A pre-tokenising scanner, compiled from the pattern string at construction
    time, replacing the regexp2 walk for every shipped encoding. An unrecognised
    pattern falls back to regexp2, so a custom encoding is slow rather than
    wrong. See core_bpe.go.

  - EncodingForModel resolves current model names (gpt-5.x, the o-series,
    Azure deployment names and ft: fine-tunes) following upstream
    openai/tiktoken's tiktoken/model.py, with longest-prefix-first matching
    because Go randomises map iteration. See encoding.go.

  - A differential equivalence gate (equiv_test.go, allenc_test.go) asserting
    byte-identical output against a verbatim copy of the pre-fork
    implementation, under all four vocabularies. The suite runs offline against
    tiktoken-go-loader's embedded vocabularies (main_test.go).

  - b.N-driven benchmarks (bench_test.go), replacing upstream's root
    benchmark_test.go, which never read b.N and therefore measured nothing.
    That file is not carried over; test/benchmark_test.go is a different
    benchmark and is kept, with its missing-corpus path changed from log.Fatal
    to b.Skip.

  - bench/, a nested module comparing this implementation against the fork-point
    implementation and against tiktoken-go/tokenizer, an independent port. It
    vendors upstream's pre-fork sources under bench/internal/upstream (MIT, see
    that directory's README) and real-text corpora under bench/testdata (see
    that directory's README for provenance and licences; the Go standard library
    source there carries Go's BSD-3-Clause licence, reproduced verbatim as
    bench/testdata/GO-LICENSE).

The model tables in encoding.go (MODEL_TO_ENCODING, MODEL_PREFIX_TO_ENCODING)
are derived from openai/tiktoken's tiktoken/model.py:

